What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dfs_enabled
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Linux kernel mailing list <linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
                Locally acknowledged firmware request-enable state.
                Writing 0 requires current frequency 640 MHz and a successful
                same-rate pin before globally inhibiting DFS requests,
                including requests from other firmware peers. Writing 1
                restores request acceptance and retains the AP 640 MHz lock.
                This does not restore the previous autonomous frequency policy
                or establish hardware quiescence. Frequency queries and rate
                requests are refused locally while disabled. Transport errors
                require recovery; requests are not retried automatically.
